  "name": "add_theory",
  "arguments": {
    "claim": "Developing a differentiated consumer proposition for a specific use case, such as smart home integration or circular economy-focused solutions, could significantly increase Biesse's market share and revenue. This is because it addresses emerging trends among individual buyers in the wood, glass, stone, and advanced materials industries, who are increasingly seeking technology-driven, sustainable, and connected tools.",
    "who_benefits": "Biesse S.p.A.",
    "why_behaviour_changes": "Emerging trends in individual buyer behavior include a growing demand for smart home integration, circular economy solutions, and sustainable, connected products. These trends present opportunities to differentiate Biesse's existing product",
    "how_value_is_captured": "By offering products that meet these emerging demands, Biesse can command premium pricing, attract new customers, and strengthen customer loyalty. Additionally, it can expand its market reach into new segments, such as smart home technology",
    "assumptions": [
      "Biesse's current product lines do not significantly incorporate smart home or circular economy features.",
      "There is a market demand for smart home integrated and circular economy-focused wood processing machines.",
      "Biesse has the technical expertise and manufacturing capabilities to develop such products."
    ],
    "predictions": [
      "A 10% increase in market share within the wood processing segment within 2 years of launching a differentiated product.",
      "A 15% increase in average order value for wood processing machines.",
      "A 20% increase in customer loyalty among new and existing customers who purchase the differentiated product."
    ]
  }
}

